# Build context exclusions. Anything the runtime does not need stays out, so
# the context stays small and changing it never invalidates a build layer.
#
# `dsl/` and `bin/` are development tooling (the YAML DSL and its code
# generator) and are deliberately absent from the image — nothing at runtime
# reads them. `scripts/` IS included: allowlist administration has no HTTP
# route on purpose, so `scripts/seed_allowed_email.py` and
# `scripts/remove_allowed_email.py` are the operator's only tools and must be
# reachable via `docker exec` (see docs/release.md). The DSL generator scripts
# ride along in the same directory: nothing executes them at runtime, and their
# pyyaml dependency stays dev-only. `alembic.ini` and
# `src/caramello_api/migrations/` are included too, because entrypoint.sh runs
# `alembic upgrade head` at boot.
.venv
.pgembed-data
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
__pycache__
*.pyc
.git
.env
.env.*
data
tests
.planning
docs
dsl
bin
compose.yaml
compose.override.yaml
